cat << 'EOF' > public/privacy-policy.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Privacy Policy - SafePass</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", 
Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; 
margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 20px; color: #333; }
        h1 { border-bottom: 2px solid #eaeaea; padding-bottom: 10px; }
        h2 { margin-top: 30px; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Privacy Policy for SafePass</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated: October 2026</strong></p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>When you log in to SafePass using Google, we request access to your 
Google account information, specifically your name, email address, and 
profile picture. We do not request or collect any sensitive personal 
data.</p>

    <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>The information collected is used strictly for the following 
purposes:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>To authenticate your identity and allow you to log in to our 
platform.</li>
        <li>To manage your account, ticket purchases, and event 
registrations.</li>
        <li>To send you transactional emails related to your tickets.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
    <p>SafePass will not share, sell, or rent your personal information to 
any third parties. Your data is used exclusively for the functionality of 
the SafePass application.</p>

    <h2>4. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
    <p>We retain your profile data as long as your account is active. If 
you wish to revoke access or request the complete deletion of your data 
